# The native core shell from flake.nix, deliberately not the default MinGW one.
#
# That shell exports CXX=x86_64-w64-mingw32-g++, and CMake takes the target
# platform from CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME rather than from the compiler -- so a core
# build there configures clean, reports a native Linux build, and quietly emits
# Windows objects. The platform-boundary check stops checking anything, without
# saying so. Nothing in CMake catches it: CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING is only true when
# CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME was set manually, which no nix shell does (nixpkgs#25477).
#
# The Windows build does not need this shell. cmake/toolchain-mingw.cmake sets
# CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME and names the compilers itself, so it only needs the cross
# toolchain on PATH, exactly as CI invokes it:
#
#   nix develop --command cmake -B build -G Ninja \
#     -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=cmake/toolchain-mingw.cmake
use flake .#core
